    "Previous Page": {
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "上一页"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Proof. Let φ(x) = f(x) − f(a) − (f(b) − f(a)) / (b − a) · (x − a). Then φ is continuous on [a, b], differentiable on (a, b), and φ(a) = φ(b) = 0. By Rolle's theorem there is ξ in (a, b) with φ′(ξ) = 0, which is the claim.": {
      "extractionState": "stale",
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "证 作辅助函数 φ(x) = f(x) − f(a) − (f(b) − f(a)) / (b − a) · (x − a)。则 φ 在 [a, b] 上连续，在 (a, b) 内可导，且 φ(a) = φ(b) = 0。由罗尔定理，存在 ξ ∈ (a, b) 使 φ′(ξ) = 0，即得所证。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Q3 2026 Business Review": {
      "extractionState": "stale",
      "localizations": {
        "zh-Hans": {
